libhybris: Android 9 / musl / X11 support for the Samsung Galaxy S8 (Exynos 8895, Mali-G71)

Base: https://github.com/libhybris/libhybris commit 60100a70f03d91224340d0b7e741e6f44e0f9618
      ("hybris: gles: Add wrappers for OpenGL ES 3.1 and 3.2", 2020-04-29)

Apply from the libhybris checkout root:
    git apply --check libhybris-android9-musl-x11.patch && git apply libhybris-android9-musl-x11.patch
then configure in hybris/ with --enable-x11 (see scripts/build-libhybris.sh).

Contents:
  * musl compatibility for hooks, properties and the mm/n/o Android linkers
    (based on postmarketOS' "Make libhybris compile with musl"; adds the
    hybris/include/hybris/common/musl_compat.h shim it relies on).
  * HYBRIS_PTHREAD_KEY_ZERO_VALID, HYBRIS_FORCE_LEGACY_PROPERTIES and
    HYBRIS_GRALLOC1_RELEASE_IMPLY_DELETE opt-in quirks for Samsung's blobs.
  * Android 9 ANativeWindow operations (SET_USAGE64, GET_CONSUMER_USAGE64,
    MAX_BUFFER_COUNT) and HYBRIS_WINDOW_DEBUG tracing.
  * X11 EGL platform (--enable-x11): gralloc buffers presented through
    DRI-hybris/Present when available, otherwise MIT-SHM/XPutImage copies.
  * eglGetConfigAttrib routed through the platform so EGL_NATIVE_VISUAL_ID
    matches the X visual.

